```rust
fn assign_project_to_customer(customer_id: u64, project_id: u64) { ... }

fn add_user_to_group(user: String, group: String) { ... }

// Call sites: swapped arguments compile successfully.
assign_project_to_customer(project_id, customer_id);
add_user_to_group("root-users".to_string(), "alice".to_string());
```

fix:
Wrap each role in a distinct nominal newtype, especially entity-specific ID types, so the compiler rejects cross-role assignment. A named argument struct can clarify positional roles, but only typed fields (not fields retaining the same primitive, nor type aliases) make the compiler reject a swap.
```rust
struct CustomerId(pub u64);
struct ProjectId(pub u64);

fn assign_project_to_customer(customer_id: CustomerId, project_id: ProjectId) { ... }

struct User(String);
struct Group(String);

fn add_user_to_group(user: User, group: Group) { ... }
```
